{{!
    @template enrol_apply/application_navigation

    Links to the applications either side of the one being reviewed.

    Both links carry the applicant's name as visible text, which is already the accessible name,
    so neither needs a title or an aria-label. The arrow beside each is decorative: with no third
    argument to the pix helper the alt is empty, and pix_icon's constructor then sets aria-hidden.

    The markup is shaped on mod_book's navigation but does not copy its btn-previous and btn-next
    class names, which are defined only in mod/book/styles.css under .path-mod-book and would
    style nothing here. What they carry there is the right-to-left flip for the chevrons; this
    plugin's stylesheet carries that rule instead, keyed on the wrapper class below.

    The way back to the queue comes first, a plain link flush with the boxes below; previous and
    next sit together on the right, next as the page's one dark pill. Without a queue link the
    first neighbour link takes the free space instead, so next stays on the right.

    The whole landmark is omitted when there is nothing to link to, so a screen reader does not
    announce an empty navigation region. It is not gated on the neighbours alone: the queue link
    has to survive a queue of one, which is when a reader most needs the way back.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * navlabel string - accessible name of the navigation landmark
    * hasnav boolean - whether there is anything to link to at all
    * previous object - the earlier application, absent at the start of the queue, carrying:
      * title string - the link's whole text, naming the applicant, plain spelling
      * url string - review page of that application
    * next object - the later application, absent at the end of the queue, same two keys
    * hasqueueurl boolean - whether this operator may open the queue this walk runs in
    * queuelabel string - text of the link back to that queue
    * queueurl string - the queue's own page

    Example context (json):
    {
        "navlabel": "Applications awaiting a decision",
        "hasnav": true,
        "hasqueueurl": true,
        "queuelabel": "All applications",
        "queueurl": "https://example.com/enrol/apply/manage.php?id=7",
        "previous": {
            "title": "Previous: Alice Anderson",
            "url": "https://example.com/enrol/apply/manage.php?userenrol=41"
        },
        "next": {
            "title": "Next: Bob Brown",
            "url": "https://example.com/enrol/apply/manage.php?userenrol=43"
        }
    }
}}
{{#hasnav}}
<nav class="enrol_apply-applicationnav" aria-label="{{navlabel}}">
    <div class="d-flex flex-wrap align-items-center gap-2">
        {{#hasqueueurl}}
            <a class="enrol_apply-navqueue me-auto" href="{{queueurl}}">{{queuelabel}}</a>
        {{/hasqueueurl}}
        {{#previous}}
            <a class="btn btn-link enrol_apply-navprevious{{^hasqueueurl}} me-auto{{/hasqueueurl}}" href="{{url}}">
                {{#pix}} i/previous, core {{/pix}}
                {{title}}
            </a>
        {{/previous}}
        {{#next}}
            <a class="btn btn-link enrol_apply-navnext{{^hasqueueurl}}{{^previous}} ms-auto{{/previous}}{{/hasqueueurl}}" href="{{url}}">
                {{title}}
                {{#pix}} i/next, core {{/pix}}
            </a>
        {{/next}}
    </div>
</nav>
{{/hasnav}}
